# Keep the build context to sources. Without this, a developer's incremental state travels into the image
# and `tsc -b` reads it as "already built" — the CE image build then reports success WITHOUT TYPECHECKING
# ANYTHING. Measured (#622 investigation): the same commit built clean with a local tsbuildinfo present and
# produced twenty errors without it. CI checks out fresh and was never fooled; a developer running the same
# command locally was.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo

# Not build inputs, and the largest things in the tree.
.git
test-results
playwright-report
**/coverage
